2026-11-07T11:51:12.6368992Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-07T11:51:12.6377578Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-07T11:51:12.6378290Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-07T11:51:12.6378774Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-07T11:51:12.6379040Z 
2026-11-07T11:51:12.6379323Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-07T11:51:12.6379650Z 
2026-11-07T11:51:12.6379914Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-07T11:51:12.6380400Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-07T11:51:12.6380638Z 
2026-11-07T11:51:12.6380839Z If you would like to
2026-11-07T11:51:12.6381395Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-07T11:51:12.6381678Z 
2026-11-07T11:51:12.6381913Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-07T11:51:12.6382455Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-11-07T11:51:12.6382650Z 
